---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About ExamCheatSheets"
  description="Learn about ExamCheatSheets — free, no-login cheat sheets and MCQs for CS exams like C-CAT and GATE CSE."
  type="website"
>
  <div class="about-page">
    <h1>About ExamCheatSheets</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      ExamCheatSheets is a free, open-source resource for students preparing for technical exams 
      in computer science. No login, no paywall, no ads.
    </p>

    <h2>What we do</h2>
    <p>
      We create scannable, accuracy-checked cheat sheets designed for the final revision stretch 
      before your exam — not for starting from zero. Every cheat sheet is paired with practice 
      MCQs and flashcards so you can test your recall immediately.
    </p>

    <h2>Exams we cover</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>C-CAT</strong> — CDAC Common Admission Test (C Programming, Data Structures, OS, Networks, DBMS, C++, Quant, AI/ML, Big Data)</li>
      <li><strong>GATE CSE</strong> — Graduate Aptitude Test in Engineering, Computer Science stream (13 subjects from Engineering Mathematics to Web Technologies)</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Open Source</h2>
    <p>
      This site is built with <a href="https://astro.build">Astro</a> and hosted on Vercel. 
      The source code is available on <a href="https://github.com/bitwiseanand/ccat">GitHub</a>. 
      Contributions, corrections, and new content are welcome.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Found an error? Have a suggestion? <a href="/contact/">Get in touch</a> or open an issue on GitHub.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-page { max-width: 720px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .about-page h1 { font-size: 2.5rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .lead {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    color: #475569;
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }
  .about-page h2 {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    font-size: 1.4rem;
  }
  .about-page ul { padding-left: 1.5rem; }
  .about-page li { margin: 0.5rem 0; }
</style>
